   "source": {
    "label": "thm:errorup",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Suppose that $\\Wcal$ is a subset of the unit Euclidean ball $\\{\\bw:\\norm{\\bw}_2\\leq 1\\}$, and contains $\\{-\\mu,\\mu\\}^d$ for some $\\mu>0$. Then for any distribution over loss vectors $\\bx$, such that $\\E[\\norm{\\bx}_2^2]\\leq c^2$ and with mean $\\bar{\\bx}$, the player strategy described above satisfies \\[ \\E\\left[\\inner{\\bar{\\bx},\\hat{\\bw}}\\right]-\\min_{\\bw\\in\\Wcal}\\inner{\\bar{\\bx},\\bw} \\leq 2c\\sqrt{\\frac{d}{T}}. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Error of returned point (simple regret analogue). Computing argmin over W assumed; compute not stated."
  },
